{#- A map hub's cards: every other solver page in the hub's folder, in
    `solverOrder`, each with its `hubLine` (or `description`). Built from those
    pages' front matter by build_scripts/eleventy/solver-index.cjs, so a new
    solver page appears here by existing.

    The name is a real <h2> inside the anchor, so puzzle names stay in the
    outline. The line is a <span>, not a <p>: line-flagger decorates
    `.content-container p`, and a flag button inside an anchor would navigate
    the moment it was clicked. -#}
<div class="content-container">
    <div class="solver-hub">
        {%- for s in collections.solverPages | solverSpokes(page.url) %}
        <a class="solver-hub__card" data-prefetchable href="{{ s.url | cleanUrl }}">
            <h2 class="solver-hub__name">{{ s.data.solverTitle }}</h2>
            <span class="solver-hub__line">{{ s.data.hubLine or s.data.description }}</span>
        </a>
        {%- endfor %}
    </div>
</div>
